    "## Section 5 — Train / Test Split\n",
    "We divide data into:\n",
    "- **Training set (80%):** The model learns from this data\n",
    "- **Test set (20%):** Used only to evaluate performance — never used for training\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why split by nodule, not by slice?\n",
    "If the same nodule appeared in both sets, the model would have seen test data\n",
    "during training, making accuracy artificially high. This is called **data leakage**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What is stratification?\n",
    "Ensures both sets have the same proportion of benign and malignant nodules\n",
    "as the full dataset. Without it, you might accidentally put most malignant\n",
    "nodules in one set.\n"
   ]
