    "## Section 8 — Training Loop\n",
    "\n",
    "### How training works (one batch):\n",
    "1. **Forward pass:** Feed inputs through the model to get predictions\n",
    "2. **Loss calculation:** Compare predictions to true labels\n",
    "3. **Backward pass:** Calculate how much each weight contributed to the error\n",
    "4. **Weight update:** Adjust weights to reduce the error\n",
    "\n",
    "This repeats for every batch = one epoch. After each epoch the model\n",
    "is evaluated on the test set (no weight updates during evaluation).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Early Stopping\n",
    "If test loss does not improve for EARLY_STOP_PAT consecutive epochs, training\n",
    "stops and the best saved model is used for evaluation.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What is loss?\n",
    "Loss measures how wrong the model's predictions are. A perfect model has\n",
    "loss = 0. The goal of training is to minimize loss on the test set.\n"
